    <briefdescription>
<para>Unscaled probability weight. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Probability weight for an edge in the graph (including the successor/target node).</para>
<para>All edges in the original function are 32-bit. However, exit edges from loop packages are taken from 64-bit exit masses, so we need 64-bits of space in general.</para>
<para>In addition to the raw weight amount, <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_block_frequency_info_impl_base_1_1_weight" kindref="compound">Weight</ref> stores the type of the edge in the current context (i.e., the context of the loop being processed). Is this a local edge within the loop, an exit from the loop, or a backedge to the loop header? </para>
    </detaileddescription>
